{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaBrowse is an audio, MIDI, FX, instrument, and action browser for REAPER. This release supports Windows x64 and requires ReaImGui 0.9 or newer.\par}
}

{\rtf1\ansi\deff0{\fonttbl{\f0 \fswiss Helvetica;}{\f1 \fmodern Courier;}}
{\colortbl;\red255\green0\blue0;\red0\green0\blue255;}
\widowctrl\hyphauto

{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel0 \b \fs36 ReaBrowse\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaBrowse is a fast audio, MIDI, FX, instrument, and action browser for REAPER. It provides native preview playback, tempo and key synchronization, library search, tags, favorites, classification, and drag-and-drop workflows.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository is the official ReaPack distribution source for ReaBrowse.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Requirements\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab Windows x64\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab REAPER\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab ReaImGui 0.9 or newer\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 MIDI audition requires a selected REAPER track containing an instrument.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Install with ReaPack\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 1.\tx360\tab In REAPER, open {\b Extensions > ReaPack > Import repositories}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 2.\tx360\tab Import this URL:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi0 \f1 https://raw.githubusercontent.com/davvolinni-ui/ReaBrowse/main/index.xml\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 3.\tx360\tab Synchronize packages.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 4.\tx360\tab Find and install {\b ReaBrowse}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 5.\tx360\tab Restart REAPER so the native companion extension is loaded.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li360 \fi-360 6.\tx360\tab Open the Action List and run {\b ReaBrowse}.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaPack installs the main script and runtime files under {\f1 Scripts/ReaBrowse} and the native companion under {\f1 UserPlugins}.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Release status\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The current package is a release candidate. Back up important REAPER settings and project data before testing prerelease software.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 Support\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Questions, bug reports, and release discussion:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?p=2958956#post2958956"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Official ReaBrowse support thread
}}}
\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 License\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 ReaBrowse is distributed under its included {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ReaBrowse/EULA.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
EULA
}}}
. Bundled third-party components retain their respective licenses and notices as documented in {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "ReaBrowse/THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
}}}
.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 This repository does not grant an open-source license to ReaBrowse merely by making its distribution files publicly accessible.\par}
}
